 "rai:dataCollection": "Records come from public datasets (provenance.json): Turkish shopping, film and supplement reviews (Turkish NLP Suite), patients' questions from doktorsitesi.com, Turkish theses' Turkish and English abstracts (YÖK), Turkish news (TRNEWS-2025), MASSIVE voice-assistant requests (tr-TR, en-US), Amazon Reviews 2023 (three categories or category groups) and English Wikinews. Nothing was collected from people for this dataset. Documents join records with synthetic user ids and dates.",
 "rai:dataCollectionType": [
  "Secondary data analysis",
  "Web scraping (by the source datasets)"
 ],
 "rai:dataPreprocessingProtocol": "CONSTRUCTION.md, section 1: HTML and whitespace cleaning; length limits; removal of reviews that state their own score; removal of texts with two labels; language filtering; set-specific rules found by profiling without labels (personal names in doctor questions; site text, cut-off fragments and typography in news; front matter and garbled text in thesis abstracts; wiki markup). Answers are computed from the source labels and recomputed by an independent script.",
 "rai:dataAnnotationProtocol": "Labels are the sources' own labels (ratings, news sections, the specialty of the doctor the patient addressed (a routing label, not a diagnosis), thesis subjects, Wikinews categories, MASSIVE scenarios), grouped as in label_maps.json. Before a set entered, native speakers labelled 20-48 sampled records blind and were then shown the source label; a set entered if each annotator agreed on at least 85% of the records they could decide and was unsure on at most 25% (70% when the checks started). Results per set are in the card.",
 "rai:dataAnnotationPlatform": "A private web page for blind labelling (source label shown only after an answer).",
 "rai:annotatorDemographics": "Native Turkish speakers: the dataset's author and two of the author's siblings, paid, blind to the source labels and to each other's answers; related to the author (disclosed).",
 "rai:dataLimitations": "Source labels are noisy (blind agreement 86-100% per set; some labels are wrong). Label checks used small samples (20-48 records per set) by annotators related to the author. Documents are synthetic arrangements of unrelated records; some question types can be answered from a sample of the records or from metadata alone; word-statistics readers score well on easy question types. Comparable Turkish-English pairs differ in sources, years and lengths; only MASSIVE and the thesis abstracts are parallel, and the thesis abstracts' semantic equivalence is unverified. No model results yet.",
 "rai:dataBiases": "Topics and styles follow the sources: Turkish e-commerce and film sites, one Turkish doctor-question site, Turkish news sites, YÖK theses from 2005 on, US Amazon reviews, English Wikinews. Label mixes in documents are random, not the sources' distributions. Sentiment sets exclude middle ratings.",
 "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "doktor_tr contains patients' questions about their health. Known-name patterns were removed (doctors' names replaced, other known first names removed, questions with e-mail addresses or self-introductions dropped); residual identifiers and linkable health narratives may remain. No consent was obtained from the writers and no ethics review was performed; the questions were public on the source site. User ids and dates in documents are synthetic. Other sets are public reviews, news, abstracts and requests.",
 "rai:dataUseCases": "Evaluating long-context aggregation (classify every record, then count, compare or rank) in Turkish and English, per question type and length; Turkish-English comparisons on the parallel sets. Not for training models to be evaluated on it, for medical advice, or for profiling the writers.",
 "rai:dataSocialImpact": "Adds Turkish to long-context evaluation, where it has been missing. Health questions could be misused to identify writers; removal requests are honoured in the next version.",
 "rai:hasSyntheticData": true,
 "rai:dataReleaseMaintenancePlan": "Versioned releases on the Hugging Face Hub (files never changed in place; a new version for every change). Maintainer: Yiğit Ateş. Removal requests privately by e-mail to yigitates1709@gmail.com (reply within 14 days; confirmed records removed in the next version, and earlier versions that contain them taken down). Generation code available to reviewers with the paper's submission and published with the paper.",
